From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: lpass-macro, soundwire: qcom: make the remove paths work

Nothing unbinds these drivers on a Qualcomm SoC, so their remove paths have
never run. Once the LPASS macro codecs are linked to the audio DSP that
provides their clocks, a DSP restart unbinds and rebinds the whole stack, and
three latent bugs surface at once.

**The clock registration leaks.** wsa_macro registers its mclk output with
clk_hw_register() where va, rx and tx all use devm_clk_hw_register(), so it is
never unregistered. The next probe then trips over the name it left behind:

    wsa_macro 6aa0000.codec: error -EEXIST: failed to register clk 'wsa2-mclk'
    wsa_macro 6aa0000.codec: probe with driver wsa_macro failed with error -17

Both wsa_macro instances stay unbound and the sound card never appears.

**Runtime PM is left enabled.** No remove calls pm_runtime_disable(), so the
next probe complains and the device starts from a stale state:

    va_macro 6d44000.codec: Unbalanced pm_runtime_enable!

**Every runtime-managed clock is disabled twice.** __device_release_driver()
runtime-suspends a device before calling .remove():

    pm_runtime_put_sync(dev);        /* runtime suspend drops the clocks */
    device_remove(dev);              /* .remove() drops them again */

so remove double-disables everything its runtime_suspend already released,
giving a WARN per clock per unbind:

    LPASS_CLK_ID_WSA2_CORE_TX_MCLK already disabled
    LPASS_CLK_ID_WSA2_CORE_TX_MCLK already unprepared

and the same in qcom_swrm_remove() for hclk, which is where it is loudest
because panic_on_warn turns it into a panic. Nothing is corrupted --
clk_core_disable() returns before decrementing -- but it is a genuine
imbalance.

Disable runtime PM first, drop the runtime-managed clocks only when the device
is not already suspended, and mark it suspended for the next probe. The clocks
taken in probe and never touched by runtime PM -- macro and dcodec, and
va_macro's equivalents -- are still released unconditionally.

Applies on top of the patch that links the macros to their clock provider;
without it none of these paths are reachable.

Rebased onto cachyos-7.3.0-2, which converted all four macros to pm_clk,
devm_pm_runtime_enable() and devm_clk_hw_register(): the macro half is
upstream's now, only the soundwire hclk fix is left.

---
diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 55678a30c..b69c67520 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1716,7 +1716,15 @@ static void qcom_swrm_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl = dev_get_drvdata(&pdev->dev);
 
 	sdw_bus_master_delete(&ctrl->bus);
-	clk_disable_unprepare(ctrl->hclk);
+
+	/*
+	 * The driver core runtime-suspends a device before calling .remove(),
+	 * and swrm_runtime_suspend() has then already dropped hclk.
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
+	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(&pdev->dev))
+		clk_disable_unprepare(ctrl->hclk);
+	pm_runtime_set_suspended(&pdev->dev);
 }
 
 static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
